E-12.verbatim_span:
fit each distribution in [genextreme, weibull min, weibull max, gumbel r, gumbel l, norm, lognorm, t, genpareto, chi, gamma,  pearson3, exponpow]
    \begin{itemize}
        \item  considering boxcox and standardization transformations
        \item  for distributions defined over zero to infinity
        \begin{itemize}
            \item trial an upper bound by subtracting the upper limit and multiplying the result by -1 (applied to peak surge for rain events and total precipitation for surge events)
            \item trial a lower bound by subtracting the lower limit (applied to total rain depth for rain events and combined events, peak surge for surge events and combined events)
        \end{itemize}
        \item  for distributions whose lower bound is controlled by the loc parameter, trial lower bound by assigning it as the loc parameter (applied to total rain depth for rain events and combined events, peak surge for surge events and combined events)
    \end{itemize}
    \item Return the p-value of the Cramer-von Mises (CVM) goodness of fit test and the Kolmogorov-Smirnov goodness of fit test, and relative goodness-of-fit metrics, the Akaike information criterion, the Bayesian information criterion, the mean square deviation index, and the mean absolute deviation index (equations for the latter 2 metrics are defined in \cite{teegavarapu_chapter_2019}).

